.TH APE 1.SH NAMEape \- gibberish in the style of what it reads.SH SYNOPSIS\fBape\fR[\-b=n[k]] [\-l=n] < source > output.SH DESCRIPTIONA travesty generator.\fBape\fRreads text on its standard input and writes new text in the same style:each character is chosen so that the last few written, taken together,occurred somewhere in the source followed by that character.  The resulthas the source's words, rhythm and punctuation and makes no sense..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-b=\fIn\fRread at most\fIn\fRbytes of source, or kilobytes with\fBk\fR;\fR8k unless told..TP 12\fB\-l=\fIn\fRhow many characters must match before it follows the source; 4 unlesstold.  Smaller is wilder, larger copies longer stretches..PPFeed it varied text: a word repeated gives it nothing to vary..SH SEE ALSOnewsgen, spew